---
const team = [
  {
    name: 'Aariz Ahmed',
    role: 'Lead Photographer',
    src: '/images/about.webp',
    alt: 'Newlyweds in traditional attire embracing under twinkling lights',
    w: 900,
    h: 1350,
    offset: 'lg:mt-0',
  },
  {
    name: 'Sana Malik',
    role: 'Second Shooter',
    src: '/images/gallery-12.webp',
    alt: 'Bride and groom in traditional attire posing indoors in modern bridal fashion',
    w: 900,
    h: 1200,
    offset: 'lg:mt-12',
  },
  {
    name: 'Daniyal Raza',
    role: 'Films & Drone',
    src: '/images/gallery-13.webp',
    alt: 'Traditional couple in classic wedding attire sharing a joyful moment indoors',
    w: 900,
    h: 1200,
    offset: 'lg:mt-24',
  },
];
---

<section id="about" class="scroll-mt-24 py-[90px] lg:scroll-mt-[111px]" aria-label="About us">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 px-5 sm:px-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 class="reveal font-display text-[3.25rem] font-normal leading-[1.05] tracking-tight sm:text-[3.625rem]">
        Hi, I’m Aariz —<br />
        I don’t pose<br />
        weddings.
      </h2>
      <div class="reveal mt-6 space-y-4 text-[1.125rem] leading-relaxed text-main">
        <p>
          Eight years ago I photographed my cousin’s mehndi with a borrowed camera and
          missed half the dances because I was crying behind the lens. I’ve been chasing
          that feeling ever since — across 250+ shaadis, from Lahore marquees to Hunza valleys.
        </p>
        <p>
          My style sits between documentary and editorial: honest, unposed moments, composed
          like the magazine spreads you grew up loving. Warm skin tones, real laughter, and
          not a single awkward “stand there and smile” unless you ask for it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div id="about-more" class="space-y-4 text-[1.125rem] leading-relaxed text-main" hidden>
        <p class="pt-4">
          Every wedding gets backup cameras, lenses and cards — always. A second shooter joins
          for large multi-day celebrations, and every frame is edited in-house by me, never
          outsourced, so the gallery you receive looks like one person’s careful work. Because
          it is.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sana and Daniyal have shot beside me for five years. Between us we cover the
          bride’s room and the baraat’s entrance, the drone shot at dusk and the grandmother
          asleep in the corner — the whole day, from every angle that matters.
        </p>
      </div>

      <button type="button" id="about-more-btn" class="btn-pill reveal mt-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-more">
        Read More About Us
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 sm:gap-5">
        {team.map((t) => (
          <figure class={t.offset}>
            <p class="mb-3">
              <span class="block font-bold leading-tight text-ink">{t.name}</span>
              <span class="block text-sm text-main">{t.role}</span>
            </p>
            <img
              src={t.src}
              alt={t.alt}
              width={t.w}
              height={t.h}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="aspect-[3/4] w-full object-cover"
            />
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="reveal mt-8 font-display text-3xl italic text-ink">— Aariz Ahmed</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
